<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saffarid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saffarids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Saffarid dynasty was a Persian dynasty founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistan">Sistan</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in the ninth century by Yaqub ibn al-Layth, a former coppersmith. It conquered much of eastern Iran and challenged the authority of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>, even marching towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>. Accounts of the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> list the Saffarids among the regional powers that emerged as caliphal military control weakened.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saffarid-dynasty.jpg" alt="Saffarid dynasty" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HistoryofIran · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Saffarid_dynasty_(861%E2%80%931002).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
